% Test cases for the TENS policy (tens.le): synthetic claims, one or two per
% criterion of LCD L33802 and per payment condition of Policy Article A52520,
% each stating only what its record shows. Findings are recorded as the
% treating practitioner's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first
% query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and
% necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base tens cases includes these resources:
    tens.

the knowledge base tens cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete purchase of a two-lead TENS unit (E0720) after a 45-day trial
% for chronic knee pain from osteoarthritis: the chronic pain criteria, the
% monitored trial, the practitioner's determination of long-term benefit,
% the record the Policy Article lists, the order and the delivery.
scenario purchase_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "physical therapy and anti-inflammatory drugs gave no lasting relief".
    the location of the pain of Ann is knee.
    the severity of the pain of Ann is severe.
    the pain of Ann has been present for 8 months.
    the presumed etiology of the pain of Ann is osteoarthritis.
    the medical record of Ann documents the prior treatment of the pain and its results.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    Ann used the TENS unit on a trial basis for 45 days.
    the finding long term benefit likely about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the reevaluation of Ann at the end of the trial period documents how the unit was used and its results.
    the order for the TENS unit is dated 2026-01-05.
    the order for the TENS unit is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the TENS unit includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the TENS unit includes order date.
    the order for the TENS unit includes description of the item.
    the order for the TENS unit includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the TENS unit includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the TENS unit was communicated to the supplier on 2026-01-06.
    the TENS unit was delivered on 2026-01-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the TENS unit.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same purchase without the reevaluation at the end of the trial in the
% record: reasonable and necessary, but the Article's documentation is
% incomplete.
scenario purchase_no_reevaluation is:
    claim 1 is for the TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "physical therapy and anti-inflammatory drugs gave no lasting relief".
    the location of the pain of Ann is knee.
    the severity of the pain of Ann is severe.
    the pain of Ann has been present for 8 months.
    the presumed etiology of the pain of Ann is osteoarthritis.
    the medical record of Ann documents the prior treatment of the pain and its results.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    Ann used the TENS unit on a trial basis for 45 days.
    the finding long term benefit likely about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the TENS unit is dated 2026-01-05.
    the order for the TENS unit is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the TENS unit includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the TENS unit includes order date.
    the order for the TENS unit includes description of the item.
    the order for the TENS unit includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the TENS unit includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the TENS unit was communicated to the supplier on 2026-01-06.
    the TENS unit was delivered on 2026-01-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the TENS unit.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the reevaluation of Ann at the end of the trial period documents how the unit was used and its results"]].

% Acute post-operative pain: a one-month rental starting four days after the
% surgery is covered (claim 1); one starting 45 days after it is not
% (claim 2).
scenario acute_post_operative is:
    claim 1 is for the TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Ben.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-05.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    Ben has acute post-operative pain from surgery on 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for the late TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the late TENS unit is "E0720".
    the late TENS unit is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-04-15.
    the order for the late TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    Cy has acute post-operative pain from surgery on 2026-03-01.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

