% A trial for shoulder pain present for two months: not yet chronic in the
% LCD's sense (three months).
scenario pain_too_recent is:
    claim 1 is for the TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the location of the pain of Eve is shoulder.
    the pain of Eve has been present for 2 months.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Four-lead units (E0730) on trial ordered for use with four leads: covered
% when the record says why two leads are insufficient (claim 1), not
% otherwise (claim 2).
scenario four_leads is:
    claim 1 is for the four lead unit.
    the HCPCS code of the four lead unit is "E0730".
    the four lead unit is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the four lead unit is ordered for use with 4 leads.
    the order for the four lead unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the trial of the four lead unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    the medical record documents why two leads are insufficient for Fay.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the location of the pain of Fay is neck.
    the pain of Fay has been present for 6 months.
    claim 2 is for the other four lead unit.
    the HCPCS code of the other four lead unit is "E0730".
    the other four lead unit is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the other four lead unit is ordered for use with 4 leads.
    the order for the other four lead unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the trial of the other four lead unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the location of the pain of Gus is neck.
    the pain of Gus has been present for 6 months.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Supplies of a purchased two-lead unit: one supply allowance (A4595) for a
% month is within the usual maximum (claim 1), two are not (claim 2); lead
% wires (A4557) seven months after the unit was delivered are too soon
% (claim 3).
scenario supplies is:
    claim 1 is for the supply allowance.
    the HCPCS code of the supply allowance is "A4595".
    the supply allowance is an accessory of the TENS unit.
    the supply allowance is furnished to Hal.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 1.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 2 is for the double supply allowance.
    the HCPCS code of the double supply allowance is "A4595".
    the double supply allowance is an accessory of the TENS unit.
    the double supply allowance is furnished to Hal.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 2.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 3 is for the lead wires.
    the HCPCS code of the lead wires is "A4557".
    the lead wires is an accessory of the TENS unit.
    the lead wires is furnished to Hal.
    the date of service of claim 3 is 2026-08-10.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Hal.
    the TENS unit was delivered on 2026-01-10.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the location of the pain of Hal is knee.
    the pain of Hal has been present for 8 months.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    Hal used the TENS unit on a trial basis for 40 days.
    the finding long term benefit likely about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A conductive garment (E0731) during the trial of a covered unit, for sites
% conventional electrodes cannot reach, but with no skin problem documented
% before the trial: not covered.
scenario garment_during_trial is:
    claim 1 is for the conductive garment.
    the HCPCS code of the conductive garment is "E0731".
    the conductive garment is an accessory of the TENS unit.
    the conductive garment is furnished to Ida.
    the conductive garment is prescribed by the treating practitioner for use in delivering covered TENS treatment.
    the finding conductive garment medically indicated about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the sites to be stimulated are inaccessible with conventional electrodes".
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Ida.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the location of the pain of Ida is back of the shoulder.
    the pain of Ida has been present for 5 months.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% The Council finds the record does not show that other treatment modalities
% were tried and failed: the purchase is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_modalities_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the TENS unit.
    the HCPCS code of the TENS unit is "E0720".
    the TENS unit is furnished to Jo.
    the order for the TENS unit was written by the treating practitioner for the condition justifying the need.
    the finding pain etiology responds to stimulation about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding other treatment modalities failed about Jo is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record mentions only a prescription for an analgesic, with no note of its trial or its result".
    the location of the pain of Jo is knee.
    the pain of Jo has been present for 10 months.
    the trial of the TENS unit is monitored by the treating practitioner.
    Jo used the TENS unit on a trial basis for 35 days.
    the finding long term benefit likely about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
